    why: 'Lenain dots his Hebrew above the letter bodies, not within them and not beneath. Those dots are encoded here as U+05C4 HEBREW MARK UPPER DOT, which is what that position means; whether he intended the biblical punctum extraordinarium or a device of his own is not something the type can settle.',
  },
